  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building the adaptive capacity and resilience of pastoral and agropastoral communities to climate shocks in Somali region of Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to pilot the roll out of the Transhumance Tracking Tool (TTT) in Dollo and Shabelle Zones of Somali region, Ethiopia, to strengthen the evidence base of life-saving humanitarian action while enhancing the adaptive capacities and resilience of pastoral and agro-pastoral communities affected by climate shocks and stresses. The piloting of the TTT system in drought and flood-prone woredas of Somali region will involve initial primary and secondary research to identify convergence zones to set up Pastoral Mobility Tracking Points (PMTP) (Phase 1), establishment of a Pastoral Flow Monitoring Network (Phase 2), data collection and analysis on herder flows, weather, conflict and route accessibility (Phase 3), and then interpretation and visualization data publication (Phase 4).</narrative>
  </description>
